    "body": "176 files, **\u22125,589 lines**, +16. **Worth reading commit-by-commit rather than as\na single diff** \u2014 the commits are deliberately ordered so each is independently\ncheckable, and squashing them together makes the reasoning impossible to follow.\n\n| area | files | removed |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| `src/web` | 52 | \u22121,678 |\n| `src/language` | 38 | \u22121,213 |\n| `src/haz3lcore` | 35 | \u22121,058 |\n| `src/pretty` | 14 | \u2212880 |\n| `src/util` | 20 | \u2212607 |\n| `test` | 13 | \u2212119 |\n| `src/CLI`, `src/menhirParser`, dune/opam | 4 | \u221234 |\n\n## Kept at reviewer request\n\nReview round 1 did exactly what the PR asked for \u2014 people recognised things they\nwanted. **19 definitions across 12 files are restored** in \"Restore definitions\nreviewers asked to keep\". They are listed here rather than tracked by the\ndetector, so this table is the record: `make dead-code` reports every one of them\nagain, by design.\n\n| restored | file | asked by | reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `err_msg` | `language/term/InvalidOperationError.re` | @Negabinary | \"wanna use it shortly\" |\n| `fresh` | `language/term/MPat.re` | @Negabinary | `MPat` was the only term module missing one |\n| `temp` \u00d73 | `language/term/{Sig,Mod,MPat}.re` | @Negabinary | same \u2014 three had lost it, not one |\n| `print_timestamp` | `util/JsUtil.re` | @Negabinary | \"don't want to look up how to do this again\" |\n| `print_time_prefix`, `print_time`, `print_times`, `measure_time` | `util/TimeUtil.re` | @Negabinary | \"looks useful\" |\n| `Debug` | `haz3lcore/projectors/implementations/ProbeProj.re` | @disconcision | \"would prefer to keep this\" |\n| `empty`, `listlit_lbl`, `mod_lbl` | `haz3lcore/lang/Token.re` | @disconcision | used in #2389 |\n| `sorted_children` | `haz3lcore/tiles/Tile.re` | @disconcision | used in #2374 |\n| `abbreviate_pat` | `language/term/Abbreviate.re` | @disconcision | used in #2115 |\n| `shard_index` | `haz3lcore/zipper/action/Indicated.re` | @disconcision | used in #1959 |\n| `to_actions` | `web/app/Log.re` | @Negabinary | wanted by the log-replay work |\n| `exercise` \u00d73 | `web/exercises/examples/Blank*Exercise.ml` | @Negabinary | **these are templates** \u2014 see below |\n\nThe `Blank*Exercise.ml` files are the one place the sweep was simply wrong. They\nwere hollowed out rather than deleted, leaving a nine-line header that ends\n*\"\u2026and edit the arguments below\"* with nothing below it. They are unreferenced\n**by design**, in the same way as the entry-point files the detector already\nexempts \u2014 a template nobody has instantiated yet has no callers and never will.\n\n## If you wanted something here, say so\n\nThe detector finds definitions with **no recorded reference**. It cannot tell rot\nfrom:\n\n- an API deliberately built out ahead of its callers,\n- an escape hatch kept around for debugging,\n- work someone has in progress on another branch and hasn't wired up yet.\n\nAll three look identical to \"dead\". Round 1 caught the items above; if there is\nmore, a comment on the relevant commit is enough, and everything here is\nrecoverable from git history.\n\n## The commits\n\n1. **Delete the dead `src/pretty` library.** 866 lines, 14 modules, zero\n   references anywhere \u2014 no `Pretty.*` use, no `open Pretty`. The apparent hits\n   are `PrettySegment`, an unrelated module in `haz3lcore`. It stayed compiled\n   only because `src/web/dune` listed it in `(libraries)`. Removing it also drops\n   **the 12 `Obj.magic` calls in `MeasuredLayout`/`Box`/`LayoutOfDoc` \u2014 the only\n   ones in the repo outside js_of_ocaml DOM interop** \u2014 and\n   `src/pretty/{ListUtil,Unicode}.re`, which duplicated `src/util` verbatim\n   because the library declared no `(libraries)` and so could not see it.\n\n2. **Empty files, orphan modules, commented-out code.** Two 1-byte files;\n   `ReadTools.re` (115 lines, never wired into `CompositionUtils.re`'s tool list\n   while its six siblings have 3-18 references each); `LogEntry`, `FailedInput`,\n   `ExerciseUtil`; and 57 consecutive commented-out lines in `CodeGrading.re`.\n\n3. **111 unused top-level definitions.** Largest: `RuleImage.of_sort` (133\n   lines), `API.node_request_streaming` (81), `Indentation.go'` (46). Densest:\n   `Icons.re` (11 unused SVG icons, including `add_file`/`add_folder`/\n   `add_project` from the removed projects UI).\n\n4. **Dead code exposed by the previous sweep**, to a fixpoint: 8 more in round\n   two, 1 in round three, 0 in round four. Notably `Sidebar.switch_assistant`,\n   whose only caller was the old assistant tab handler.\n\n5. **Dead definitions found by the index**, to a fixpoint: 3,769 lines across 134\n   files. This is the category the text scan structurally could not see \u2014 58\n   members nested inside `module X = {...}` blocks, and functions whose only\n   callers are their own recursive calls (`Segment.remold_sig_uni`,\n   `CodeExercise.append_exp`, `ValueChecker.check_value_mod_ctx`).\n\n6. **Dead types, constructors and write-only record fields** \u2014 the category the\n   index cannot see *at all*, because `[@deriving]` emits ghost occurrences for\n   every constructor at the type declaration. Found by hand, each checked\n   individually. Includes `SafeTriangle.active_state`'s\n   `exit_point`/`menu_direction`, which are written in `activate` and never read;\n   warning 69 cannot see this because they *are* written.\n\n7. **`OptUtil.filter`**, restored \u2014 it became live on `dev` while this branch was\n   open.\n\n8. **Restore definitions reviewers asked to keep** \u2014 the 19 above, plus four\n   dangling comments left behind by earlier deletions (`Typ.re`, `API.re`,\n   `TutorialGrading.re`, and an over-long rationale in\n   `Test_Evaluator_Properties.re`).\n\n## What was deliberately not deleted\n\nThe part I would most like scrutinised, because it is where judgement replaced\nmechanism.\n\n- **Anything a ppx can synthesise a call to** without it appearing in source:\n  `Sample.{show,sexp_of,\u2026}_targets`, `RichProbe.show_packed_*`,\n  `RichProbeRegistry.yojson_of_packed_action`, `ConstructorMap.equal_constructor`,\n  `Tree.equal_struct`. `Sample.re`'s are reached from `EvalInfo.re`'s\n  `[@deriving sexp]` on a `Sample.targets` field.\n- **Comment blocks that carry knowledge rather than rot**: the `pp` overrides in\n  `Annotated.re`/`IdTagged.re` are documented debugging affordances;\n  `ProofRule.re`'s disabled `BinOp` rule carries a TODO about negation and\n  implication plus a type-level sketch of an in-progress feature; `Statics.re`'s\n  `NOTE(yuchen)` documents a correctness caveat.\n- **`Test_Statics_Sums`' `badTypeName`**, reported by an earlier scan \u2014 it is\n  Hazel source inside a `{|...|}` literal, not OCaml.\n- **Seven reported definitions were false positives the build caught.** Each\n  became a suppression rule in the detector rather than a one-off exclusion.\n\n## Two things that grew coverage instead of shrinking it\n\n- `Test_Coverage`'s `nested_constructors_exhaustive` and\n  `type_function_scrutinee` are complete tests that were never added to the suite\n  list. Both pass; now registered (62 -> 64 in that suite).\n- `Test_Evaluator_Properties`' `qcheck_preservation_test` was unreferenced\n  because its registration was commented out with \"Disabled due to known issues\n  with preservation\". It is now registered as an explicit `Alcotest.skip()` so the\n  gap appears in the report instead of hiding as dead code.\n\n## One deletion worth naming\n\n**`VarBstMap`** \u2014 a 237-line module plus a 187-line `.rei` \u2014 is deleted entirely.\nIts only reference in the whole repo was\n`module M = { include VarBstMap.Ordered; };` inside a match arm of\n`Test_Grammar.re`, where `M` is then never used: a no-op that made the module look\nreachable. Flagging it because it is a documented, odoc-commented data structure,\nnot obviously junk. If anyone wants it kept as future API, this is the commit to\nobject to.\n\n## Verification\n\n`dune build @src/fmt src --profile release` \u2014 the gating CI build, where warnings\n32/33/34/37 are errors \u2014 is clean. `make test-quick`: **3,268 passing**.\n\n`make dead-code` reports **23** dead definitions in `src/`, not zero:\n\n- **19** are the restorations above, kept at reviewer request.\n- **3** arrived dead from the `dev` merge and are not this branch's to judge \u2014\n  `CLI/Run.re`'s `evaluate_with_probe_map`, `Refractors.persist`, and\n  `Token.of_projector_invoke_opt`, all landed by the fast-parse work and not yet\n  wired up.\n- **1**, `TutorialGrading.percentage_view`, is removed by #2437's\n  `include Grading;` dedup, one branch up the stack.\n\nSo the detector-zero claim from round 1 no longer holds, deliberately. Anyone\nre-running the sweep should read the table above first.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
